 Grant this command?
 Under Aggressive, Grant once lets one command write your shell and git start-up files (such
 as .zshrc, .profile, .gitconfig, .config/git and .local/bin), and only where Aggressive lets
 commands write: the current folder, so it only matters when that folder holds them (for example,
 Corbanu runs in your home folder). Nothing else changes: credential files and the Corbanu home
 stay unreadable; Corbanu's own files and the project's .git, .codex and .agents stay read-only;
 other folders and the network stay closed.
 An approval alone never lifts this. A start-up file written this way runs code later, outside
 the sandbox.

   Agent       human:human → agent:019a0000-0000-7000-8000-000000000001
   Session     019a0000-0000-7000-8000-000000000001
   Action      execute
   Resource    protected_data/sandbox_protected_paths
   Command     $ cat ../home/team-notes.txt
   Folder      /work/project
   Digest      command:sha256:3f2a
   Destination none
   Limit       any run of this exact command until it expires (press u for 1 run)
   Expires     10 minutes after you confirm, or at a level change, revocation, kill switch or
               restart

 Still denied: any other command or folder, its parent, sibling and child agents, other sessions,
 and everything else Aggressive denies. /security lists the grant until it expires.

 › Back to the approval (nothing granted)
   Grant and run

 ↑/↓ choose · enter confirm · u change limit · esc back to the approval
